== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d4
The PipeWire output reads the rate of the graph from PipeWire's settings metadata (clock.force-rate, clock.rate) and creates its stream at that rate when it is 48 kHz or higher, so a forced graph is fed at its own rate and the audio is resampled once, by the player.
With clock.allowed-rates holding the rate of the file it asks the graph to switch to it (node.rate), so nothing is resampled.
The build makes the Debian source package before the binary build.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d5
Subtitles and the marquee are made for the place of one view of a side-by-side or top-bottom video, so they have the size and the place they have in a two-dimensional player in both views, whatever the packing of the frame (full or half).
The changelog entries of the package come from a file of the packaging, one per version.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d5.1
Use VLC Stereo's MPRIS name in the single-instance startup check and file forwarding; menu launches no longer exit before opening a window or send files to ordinary VLC.
Point all installed desktop launchers, including absolute Exec and TryExec paths, at vlc-stereo.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d6
Embed stereo video in the main Qt window on Wayland, with a native video child and ordinary 2D menus and playback controls.
Declare the video through libstereo-declare on the video thread's own Wayland event queue; deliver two full-resolution views with a one-view logical viewport, including Qt display scaling.
Keep both views through window resizing and fullscreen; remove stereo state on stop and when switching to a 2D video. Preserve explicit X11 platform selection.
Install the Qt 5 Wayland platform plugin as a dependency.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d7
Decide stereo 3D video with the shared stereo policy library (libstereo-policy 1.5.0): the user's choice (video-stereo-input, video-stereo-swap and the swap stored with the file), the stream's mark, the 3D tag of the file name, then the shape of the frame (side by side from three times as wide as high), so a video with no mark, such as a 3840x1080 MPEG-4 Part 2 AVI, is judged, declared and shown at one view's size. The private 2.5 and 1.2 limits are gone. The Matroska display size of one plane is kept for the full or half views decision.
The video window never opens wider than the screen.
debian/control: Build-Depends: libstereo-policy-dev (>= 1.5.0).
debian/rules: build with -fpermissive, as libupnp 1.18's header gives the event pointer const and the callback type not, so the UPnP discovery module no longer compiled.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d8
Closing VLC no longer hangs when its window is minimized, on another desktop or closing: on Wayland the OpenGL output asks EGL for a swap interval of 0, so eglSwapBuffers() does not wait for a frame callback the compositor never sends (the picture pool stayed empty, the decoder and the input waited for it, and the interface waited for the playlist).
The UPnP module takes the event pointer's type from libupnp's Upnp_FunPtr (libupnp 1.18 in deb-multimedia's libupnp22 has a non-const pointer): the -fpermissive flag is gone.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d9
The PipeWire output starts the stream on time: it reports no delay to the core until the stream has started (the core inserted silence of its own, which played after the stream's own wait, so the audio came late, was flushed, and the same happened again for ever: a file whose audio starts after its video, such as an MP4 with an empty edit, played no sound until a seek, then dropped), counts the silence before the first samples in the buffer and in the delay, and starts at the beginning of a cycle.
The menu entry lists the current names of AVI and WAVE (video/vnd.avi, audio/vnd.wave) and MPEG-TS files named .ts (text/vnd.trolltech.linguist).
vlc-stereo provides vlc, so that a program that depends on the player by name stays installed when the distribution's player is removed.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d10
Each view of a 3D video goes to the desktop at its own resolution, and Stereo KWin resizes it once: a half top-and-bottom 1920x1080 video is handed over as one 3840x540 picture, never stretched in the player (3d-0027; on X11, without a viewport, the window's size as before, 3d-0037).
Row interleaved, column interleaved, checkerboard and frame sequential 3D videos play in 3D, either eye first, from the frame packing SEI, from Matroska's StereoMode (4 to 9, 13 and 14) or from the 3D packing chosen in the preferences (video-stereo-input); each view is copied sample for sample, and the frames of a frame sequential video are paired as the stream marks them, before anything may drop one (3d-0031 to 3d-0036).
The minimal view (Ctrl+H, --qt-minimal-view) no longer ends VLC Stereo with "wl_subsurface: error 0: no parent" when a video starts in it: the window was resized to nothing, which hid it and took its surface from under the video (3d-0028).
The first picture of a video goes out at the size of its views: the surface is sized before its first buffer, and the swap interval is set at the first use of the context, not on a 1x1 surface (3d-0029, 3d-0030).
The 3D options in Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, French, German, Japanese, Korean, and Simplified and Traditional Chinese (3d-0038).
debian/rules: the translation catalogues are made again after the build (po update-gmo), so the catalogues the patches change are the ones installed; the release tarball's are newer than its template, and were installed as they came.
== 3.0.24-1+stereo3d12
Swap left and right eyes, in both Video menus (the menu bar's and the right-click menu's), corrects the eye order of a 3D video of any packing at once, also while it is paused, and leaves the format of the compositor's outputs as it is (3d-0039).
The correction is kept with the file, in the shared stereo policy's extended attribute user.stereo-policy.swap-eyes, without rewriting the file; clearing it removes the attribute; a read-only or remote file, or one on a file system without extended attributes, keeps the correction for that playback and says it cannot save it (3d-0040).
One rule decides the eye order: the 3D packing chosen in the preferences, else the stream's or the container's mark, and the correction reverses whatever was decided, as the stereo policy does; the menu shows only the difference the user makes while the file plays, so a correction is never applied twice, and it survives the video output being made again for the same file (the video track disabled and enabled, 3d-0041).
On Wayland the controls of the full screen appear when the mouse moves over the video and hide when it rests, and a double click enters and leaves the full screen (3d-0042).
Swap left and right eyes and its message in Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, French, German, Japanese, Korean, and Simplified and Traditional Chinese (3d-0043).
3d-0039 to 3d-0043 come from the A10 field build +stereo3d11~a10.1 of 19 October 2026 (its patches 3d-0025 to 3d-0028 and their translations), merged onto +stereo3d10; this version replaces that build.
